---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ThreadPanel from '../components/ThreadPanel.astro';
import FlowRail from '../components/FlowRail.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
import Arrow from '../components/Arrow.astro';
import { pageMeta, services } from '../data/site';

const meta = pageMeta.home;
---

<BaseLayout title={meta.title} description={meta.description}>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero__rules" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="container hero__grid">
      <div>
        <h1>
          One <span class="text-teal">connected flow</span>,<br class="hero__break" />
          from CRF design to final report.
        </h1>
        <p class="hero__lede">
          SevenHills is building one end-to-end clinical data platform for CRF design, TMF, EDC,
          data management, pharmacovigilance, biostatistics, SAS analysis, and final reports. One
          record, one team, and a traceable path from the first field to the final result.
        </p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/platform/">
            Explore the platform
            <Arrow class="btn__arrow" />
          </a>
          <a class="btn btn--secondary" href="/contact/">Contact us</a>
        </div>
        <div class="hero__meta">
          <span>Product in development</span>
          <span>Scarborough, Ontario, Canada</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <ThreadPanel />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>Clinical data still moves in pieces.</h2>
        <p>
          Most clinical technology stacks grew one tool at a time. The gaps between those tools are
          where time, context, and confidence are lost.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="problem__grid">
        <article class="problem__item">
          <span class="problem__num">01</span>
          <h3>Disconnected tools</h3>
          <p>
            A form builder in one system, data capture in another, coding in a spreadsheet, and
            reporting in a separate package. Each handoff asks the same data to be entered or
            explained again.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="problem__item">
          <span class="problem__num">02</span>
          <h3>Manual data movement</h3>
          <p>
            Exports, email attachments, and reconciliation files become the connective tissue. The
            study record depends on someone remembering which version is current.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="problem__item">
          <span class="problem__num">03</span>
          <h3>Delays in trials</h3>
          <p>
            Queries and reconciliation take longer when the history is spread across systems.
            Traceability gets rebuilt after the fact, often close to a reporting deadline.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--tint flow">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="flow__head">
        <h2>Eight stages. One thread.</h2>
        <p>
          The platform is being built as one record with eight connected stages. A field defined in
          CRF design is captured once, reviewed in context, and carried through to the report.
        </p>
      </div>

      <FlowRail />

      <div class="flow__notes">
        <div class="flow__note">
          <strong>Entered once</strong>
          <span>Sites enter a value once. Downstream teams read the same record instead of a copy.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="flow__note">
          <strong>Carried forward</strong>
          <span>Field definitions, units, queries, and coding decisions travel with the data.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="flow__note">
          <strong>Traceable end to end</strong>
          <span>Every reported result can be followed back to its source, with the history intact.</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container why__grid">
      <div class="why__intro">
        <h2>Why SevenHills</h2>
        <p>
          The platform is being designed around the way clinical data actually moves, not around a
          single step in the workflow.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="why__list">
        <article class="why__item">
          <h3>Connected data</h3>
          <p>
            The same field, definition, and history move through every stage. There is no separate
            truth to reconcile at the end.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="why__item">
          <h3>Designed for validation</h3>
          <p>
            Audit trails, controlled definitions, and traceability are part of the design, not a
            layer added before an inspection.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="why__item">
          <h3>Built by clinical data professionals</h3>
          <p>
            The platform is being shaped by people who work in clinical data management, safety,
            statistics, and clinical software.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="why__item">
          <h3>One team from design to report</h3>
          <p>
            Product and services sit under one team, so the people configuring a study understand
            how it will be analyzed and reported.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--grey">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="index-head">
        <h2>Services across the clinical data lifecycle.</h2>
        <a class="text-link" href="/services/">
          View all services
          <Arrow />
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="service-index">
        {
          services.map((service) => (
            <a class="service-link" href={`/services/#service-${service.number}`}>
              <span class="service-link__num">{service.number}</span>
              <span>
                <span class="service-link__name">{service.name}</span>
                <span class="service-link__short">{service.short}</span>
              </span>
              <Arrow class="service-link__arrow" />
            </a>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand />
</BaseLayout>
